{"title":"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#I_can&#39;t_comprehend_the_end!\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">I can't comprehend the end!</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let \\(b\\ge 2\\) be an integer. Call a positive integer \\(n\\) \\(b\\text-\\textit{eautiful}\\) if it has exactly two digits when expressed in base \\(b\\)  and these two digits sum to \\(\\sqrt n\\). For example, \\(81\\) is \\(13\\text-\\textit{eautiful}\\) because \\(81  = \\underline{6} \\ \\underline{3}_{13} \\) and \\(6 + 3 =  \\sqrt{81}\\). Find the least integer \\(b\\ge 2\\) for which there are more than ten \\(b\\text-\\textit{eautiful}\\) integers.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We write the base-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> two-digit integer as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/5/43547c2e6051033a750c944af54cbe29d25c11ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( xy \\right)_b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"43\" height=\"21\" />.\nThus, this number satisfies\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/0/7302d6780f26d8bd37f87cb295b5b68eb54c94da.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\left( x + y \\right)^2 = b x + y \\]\" width=\"136\" height=\"22\" />\nwith <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/5/c154f1de658d52d3d4a1ab1ab87fd63e500e8a62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\in \\left\\{ 1, 2, \\cdots , b-1 \\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"161\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/1/ef10f2f98c1080bf75a83238e7aff8b79a65e1e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\in \\left\\{ 0, 1, \\cdots , b - 1 \\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"161\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>The above conditions imply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25d445c7aceb19b2ae825bedd5d1536b53409a6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( x + y \\right)^2 &lt; b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"23\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/c/61cc5543935aba2f5bbdb22a10f2671f39c6f702.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y \\leq b - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>The above equation can be reorganized as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/a/5aac48dbc0ff21fea008c84c6f75a381fa7d115a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\left( x + y \\right) \\left( x + y - 1 \\right) = \\left( b - 1 \\right) x . \\]\" width=\"240\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/0/4f0126bb8ba008537f5c8c8be83679d607d22720.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = x + y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/0/a20d6c7fc6bb41513734f3e57bf1a867166fb67c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&#39; = b - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" />.\nThus, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/f/c6fad82cae2d9cd61f4303c7c50384ed830353f9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ z \\left( z - 1 \\right) = b&#39; x , \\hspace{1cm} (1) \\]\" width=\"190\" height=\"18\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/1/ae1d83869123aa0b29f4e6b9def30daf4a920d9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z \\in \\left\\{ 2, 3, \\cdots , b&#39; \\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"134\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/c/b4cdbeeb55a129db991d5ee133b84890aceeba61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\in \\left\\{ 1, 2, \\cdots , b&#39; \\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"135\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Next, for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39574adf537bc19e989f7b69bee4bf19c7d7f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&#39;$\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we solve Equation (1).\n</p><p>We write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39574adf537bc19e989f7b69bee4bf19c7d7f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&#39;$\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the prime factorization form as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/3/633d17c5f508969d4e12ecc260b628dece295f60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&#39; = \\Pi_{i=1}^n p_i^{k_i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"22\" />.\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/5/0f5bb087488bdd644b7864ef920a0ef3ac24b312.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(A, \\bar A \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"53\" height=\"23\" /> be any ordered partition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/e/2be5e24f89ad9aa77f5a26a396d123dd2b2c4076.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\{ 1, 2, \\cdots , n \\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" /> (we allow one set to be empty).\nDenote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/0/47044c8d5046d949c570937782c36ae917aa11a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_A = \\Pi_{i \\in A} p_i^{k_i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"109\" height=\"22\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/1/1e1c65df670d0bcd5bcd76e3e0d83a6146e74e8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{\\bar A} = \\Pi_{i \\in \\bar A} p_i^{k_i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"109\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/5/215e7b85d1bf197bfc13a18e60c239febc3aa340.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\rm gcd} \\left( z, z-1 \\right) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"138\" height=\"20\" />, there must exist such an ordered partition, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/3/6130165562ea82413ff6318a1823fb091704592b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_A | z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/3/cb31a2648d61aa1f51ae5a71cfe4e78767685341.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{\\bar A} | z-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Next, we prove that for each ordered partition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/9/809cf0a04312bd0b4f5ecc357d60c8b7c11d8a56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( A, \\bar A \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"53\" height=\"23\" />, if a solution of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> exists, then it must be unique.\n</p><p>Suppose there are two solutions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> under partition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/9/809cf0a04312bd0b4f5ecc357d60c8b7c11d8a56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( A, \\bar A \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"53\" height=\"23\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/d/52d3d13ba328a13bf17ae2e53e982e2901ad1515.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1 = c_1 P_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/2/0c2c7e6b8994c517352bf49fcafa93fb1495f939.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1 - 1 = d_1 P_{\\bar A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/4/fa4d70256bb5c0ee12202aa0fee871f0e97f8449.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_2 = c_2 P_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/d/77ddd6ef4ac2d18ea7851b92b90a0b05b67706d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_2 - 1 = d_2 P_{\\bar A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" />.\nW.L.O.G., assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/f/0afcc7a4d55767066ba7a6ae16399e60a74d860c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_1 &lt; c_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"15\" />.\nHence, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/1/8114240bc6197357038a4ecf21305e4b103fed1c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\left( c_2 - c_1 \\right) P_A = \\left( d_2 - d_1 \\right) P_{\\bar A} . \\]\" width=\"214\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/1/c318650104a9cca369491a7f446be6326abfaa1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\rm gcd} \\left( P_A, P_{\\bar A} \\right) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/f/0afcc7a4d55767066ba7a6ae16399e60a74d860c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_1 &lt; c_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"15\" />, there exists a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/2/ae292fe85c049cf201d9496d7276c3ae0192f33c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_2 = c_1 + m P_{\\bar A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/e/1dede524664886814ee8617c882688b53e10572e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_2 = d_1 + m P_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"17\" />.\nThus,\n\\begin{align*}\nz_2 &amp; = z_1 + m P_A P_{\\bar A} \\\\\n&amp; = z_1 + m b' \\\\\n&amp; &gt; b' .\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>However, recall <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/d/2ad64e1b63fbd7aad59955d086182cbdad97ceee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_2 \\leq b&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"19\" />. We get a contradiction.\nTherefore, under each ordered partition for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39574adf537bc19e989f7b69bee4bf19c7d7f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&#39;$\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the solution of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is unique.\n</p><p>Note that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39574adf537bc19e989f7b69bee4bf19c7d7f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&#39;$\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> distinct prime factors, the number of ordered partitions is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c36f0b157e8c2fbe0638c2f2b378e08d07695aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />.\nTherefore, to find a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39574adf537bc19e989f7b69bee4bf19c7d7f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&#39;$\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> such that the number of solutions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is more than 10, the smallest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is 4.\n</p><p>With <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/5218af40079081e694d8b82eeac2d368ef6ea76a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, the smallest number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/4/1b431da81e485a80f2e5c03149dfc557a83ccbfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 7 = 210$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"129\" height=\"14\" />.\nNow, we set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/1/0c147db9cb29a7726974e2f017a2967c7df57b8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&#39; = 210$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"16\" /> and check whether the number of solutions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> under this <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39574adf537bc19e989f7b69bee4bf19c7d7f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&#39;$\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is more than 10.\n</p><p>We can easily see that all ordered partitions (except <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/e/b5e3236a24240fb6689c596f92015a9e46c9e6d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\emptyset$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />) guarantee feasible solutions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\nTherefore, we have found a valid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39574adf537bc19e989f7b69bee4bf19c7d7f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&#39;$\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\nTherefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/5/5c5608967dfccbad54f29d93781a7f0a1b21a1d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = b&#39; + 1 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(211) }}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"163\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Shen Kislay Kai and Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"I_can.27t_comprehend_the_end.21\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"I_can't_comprehend_the_end!\">I can't comprehend the end!</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: I can&#39;t comprehend the end!\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Continue until reaching <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/f/c6fad82cae2d9cd61f4303c7c50384ed830353f9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ z \\left( z - 1 \\right) = b&#39; x , \\hspace{1cm} (1) \\]\" width=\"190\" height=\"18\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/1/ae1d83869123aa0b29f4e6b9def30daf4a920d9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z \\in \\left\\{ 2, 3, \\cdots , b&#39; \\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"134\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/c/b4cdbeeb55a129db991d5ee133b84890aceeba61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\in \\left\\{ 1, 2, \\cdots , b&#39; \\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"135\" height=\"20\" />. Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must divide into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/7/60724d31afea30fd52c825bd42cd55a7805d5ad9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z(z-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"20\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/9/e99c0d4cdb3a09f763f7b9afcdf28b4102a3f7fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&#39;x = z(z-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"113\" height=\"20\" />. Then, notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/d/01d9f89911f9d15e2f896d2d24025070762d9508.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(z,z-1) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"134\" height=\"20\" />, and thus either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/0/5e0354f5222a779c87639c207f520488f84500cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x~|~ z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/5/3554d621accd0b5b402c916eebc0b1021e9d3c9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x ~ | ~ z-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Every solution then corresponds to a rough divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39574adf537bc19e989f7b69bee4bf19c7d7f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&#39;$\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39574adf537bc19e989f7b69bee4bf19c7d7f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&#39;$\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> positive prime divisors. Then, every divisor can be distributed to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50e0412f1e4c5bde18c5a76f43bd0c5256c8fb2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" />, contributing a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c36f0b157e8c2fbe0638c2f2b378e08d07695aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> choices.  To obtain more than 10 solutions, one must find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/a/81a2fe4327f65e68ee30a09343a593eef4d1fe0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n &gt; 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" />, in which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/b/d1b94ea0cc3ac2d353695f157196aed47896fefc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>The smallest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39574adf537bc19e989f7b69bee4bf19c7d7f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&#39;$\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> occurs with the four smallest prime divisors, those being, 2, 3, 5, 7, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/1/0c147db9cb29a7726974e2f017a2967c7df57b8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&#39; = 210$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"16\" />, and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/7/4a7f86665b6b6b947078051d193ba613a69b7f20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = b&#39; + 1 = \\boxed{211}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"140\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/5/69508c3442ac189d46e262653c5478ccd03602e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\le q\\le b-1, 0\\le r\\le b-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"221\" height=\"18\" />, we wish to determine the least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> such that the system\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/b/8aba7c9e0bfdff51f9e89ceee6d784c0c3d17cb9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n=qb+r, \\quad\\sqrt{n}=q+r\\]\" width=\"195\" height=\"18\" />\nhas at least 10 solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/4/5145cbbe7b62640308f127ed5a704112e45e88e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(q,r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />. Squaring the second equation, this is equivalent to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/6/2760e9d7ca1cb75039376ac84b50db389fc9992b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[q^2+2qr+r^2=qb+r\\iff r^2+(2q-1)r+q^2-qb=0\\]\" width=\"448\" height=\"20\" />\nSolving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/7/9e7bd2b3ef0110f45142097f877c6b4dce4e5ff1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r=\\frac{1}{2}-q+\\sqrt{\\frac{4q(b-1)+1}{4}}\\]\" width=\"223\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer, hence we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/6/6b63a29a391102ab0e00f052d1a9294703b4b901.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q(b-1)=x(x-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"20\" /> for integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/2/b5205f058a0f55b22ecf025f21108e6b2ed1100c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. But having established <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/6/6f679d7c352f38e41a5620f7ef6115f50b95fa1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q\\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" />, we cannot have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/8/7284a43209432ed202230527d545082dbe571ec0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0,1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"17\" />. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/e/d8ecb06996bc48860e20975f454dc107cb48fdb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=x-q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/d/ffdaee5bac3622a3b5e9a77804527f79f11475b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=b-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/2/532b31553856680ae9e00df3852f5a6f80f60567.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\ge N+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"17\" /> contradicts <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/6/f867c2b7f377c396698ca5d426be3b2e41f2349e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q\\le N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/a/5fab1da6b3c0c4116e26b67917f083d3d98bc986.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in [2, N]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" />, and we know that\n\\begin{gather*}\nr=x-q\\le x-1\\le N-1\\\\\nq=\\frac{x(x-1)}{N}\\le x-1\\implies r=x-q&gt; 0\n\\end{gather*}\n</p><p>This satisfies our initial restriction on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, which means any indices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/301650528deb3e6d87e7129c6c498822af99ae82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in[2,N]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" /> that results in an integral solution for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> holds a valid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/e/71e16b3e6a97e2e868b2b7bd855837d38b43e424.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x(x-1)\\equiv 0\\pmod{N}\\]\" width=\"187\" height=\"18\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/b/d4baf6d4b1cfa69b68b3204b5e2eba0c5755fe20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> are relatively prime, every factor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/0/4101abf229ca5198f3e9fb26f0931354f0ea5b9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_i^{e_i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/c/74ce35f31e3bc46637ded5db76392e10e2ad2b8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=\\prod_{i=1}^k p_i^{e_i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"90\" height=\"56\" /> must divide either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/b/d4baf6d4b1cfa69b68b3204b5e2eba0c5755fe20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />. Hence, by the Chinese Remainder Theorem, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/d/8cd4b77f51a75356a36c62b44a017c9cd6218c68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i\\in\\{0,1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"84\" height=\"20\" />, the system\n\\begin{align*}\nx&amp;\\equiv a_1 \\pmod{p_1^{e_1}}\\\\\nx&amp;\\equiv a_2 \\pmod{p_2^{e_2}}\\\\\n&amp;\\ldots\\\\\nx&amp;\\equiv a_k \\pmod{p_k^{e_k}}\n\\end{align*}\nhas <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/7/767b7dc4a8df95a9f8a0faa3bb155e7b49943407.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> solutions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> residue modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. However, we need to exclude the case when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dc0936b490aa8e875fba0a47e15e449ac823dfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-1 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"157\" height=\"20\" />, which yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c52e02a35db152495396584bfeae1d0599cd753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. Hence, we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/2/742961194c5ce0c45e87f015a7fa5a78c9edc06a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^k-1&gt;10\\implies k\\ge 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"186\" height=\"20\" />. The least value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> that includes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> distinct prime factor is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/4/d745df1c52d5b86bc7ab313925467aa13569625c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[N=2\\cdot 3\\cdot 5\\cdot 7=210\\]\" width=\"166\" height=\"13\" />\nTherefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/2/ec2e8667e0eeeff2f3c096531a6f5e601f865372.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=N+1=\\boxed{211}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"145\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Pieandpi31415926535897932\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/N7rLL1Xt9go\">https://youtu.be/N7rLL1Xt9go</a>\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/0FCGY9xfEq0?si=9Fu4owVaSm-WWxFJ\">https://youtu.be/0FCGY9xfEq0?si=9Fu4owVaSm-WWxFJ</a>\n</p><p>~MathProblemSolvingSkills.com\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II\" title=\"2024 AIME II\">2024 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2024 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2024\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018012101\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.061 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.083 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 662/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1810/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 132/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 20866/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.062      1 -total\n 60.02%    7.840      1 Template:AIME_box\n 38.01%    4.965      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:27007:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018012101 and revision id 290639. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}